From 73c19ec89df9c90070ca0a53fa9378bb93c87c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sak-114514 <Sak-114514@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:57:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Make AC922 TP3 inference trials reproducible without
 rewriting model files

The Qwen3.8 checkpoint has KV, GDN, MLP, and vocabulary dimensions that
cannot be divided directly across three V100s. Opt-in load-time head
replication, output-scale balancing, and zero padding preserve the source
weights while allowing the existing tensor-parallel loaders to run. The
DFlash2 drafter also needs an opt-in TP3 expansion because this fork builds
its draft with the target TP group despite accepting a TP1 draft setting.

The isolated launcher and tests keep the current installed runtime separate
from these trials. The DFlash KV planner uses a bounded common page and a
five-group layout to admit four simultaneous short requests.

Constraint: POWER9, three 16GB V100s, CUDA 12.4, and fork db292f9a4
Constraint: Original checkpoint files and production runtime package remain unchanged
Rejected: Draft TP1 config alone | model construction still uses the target TP3 group
Rejected: Draft FP8 KV as a capacity fix | draft scales are unverified and the common page does not halve
Confidence: medium
Scope-risk: moderate
Reversibility: clean
Directive: Preserve the explicit opt-in flags and the shared source-and-copy half scaling; do not infer bitwise equality from greedy parity
Tested: Seven unit and real-checkpoint checks; Ruff and shell syntax; targeted mypy; 20/20 TP2-vs-TP3 greedy outputs; 100k and 199k prefill/decode; DFlash acceptance and token-counted throughput; 1803s four-way run with 1265 successful requests and max Running=4 Waiting=0
Not-tested: Four simultaneous full-64k contexts; DFlash at 200k (rejected by measured KV budget); production switchover; full-project mypy and CI suite
